{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Hear.</b> He returns to speak with the good ones, who believe the words of the prophet." "And the meaning of <b>and look</b> is like: do not marvel how Zion shall again be full of children as she was." "<b>Look to the rock.</b> Like \"Here I am standing before you there on the rock\" (Exodus 17:6)." "<b>[you were hewn].</b> That you were hewn from it, and this is Abraham." "<b>and to the hollow of the pit.</b> From the root of \"and he bored a hole in its door\" (II Kings 12:10)." "<b>you were dug.</b> From it; this is Sarah."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 51, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:56.253216582Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}